---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SEOHead from '../components/SEOHead.astro';
---

<BaseLayout>
  <SEOHead
    slot="head"
    title="Resume | Jacob Steelsmith"
    description="Resume of Jacob Steelsmith — Staff Engineer & Engineering Manager with 20+ years of experience in cloud platforms, distributed systems, AI engineering, and technical leadership."
  />

  <h1>Resume</h1>
  <br />
  <section class="resume-section" aria-labelledby="summary-heading">
    <h2 id="summary-heading">Professional Summary</h2>
    <p>Staff-level engineer and hands-on engineering manager with over 13 years building and operating customer-facing web applications, APIs, cloud platforms, and enterprise infrastructure on AWS. Designed and delivered production systems using Python, TypeScript, JavaScript, Node.js, React, and SQL serving thousands of users. Brings end-to-end ownership across architecture, implementation, deployment, reliability, operations, and product evolution.</p>
    <p>Built and led engineering and IT teams for 11 years while remaining an active technical contributor. Proven track record transforming legacy monoliths and on-premises systems into cloud-native, serverless, and distributed architectures. Deep expertise across platform engineering, DevOps, infrastructure, real-time streaming, data platforms, security, and AI-assisted development workflows. Experienced directing IT infrastructure, cloud, security, compliance, and operational initiatives in resource-constrained environments.</p>
    <p>Known for operating effectively in ambiguous, high-pressure environments, aligning technology strategy with business outcomes, and combining strategic leadership with practical engineering execution. Strong cross-functional collaboration and a builder mindset focused on delivering scalable, maintainable systems that solve real operational problems and create value.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="resume-section" aria-labelledby="skills-heading">
    <h2 id="skills-heading">Skills</h2>

    <h3>Languages</h3>
    <ul class="skill-list">
      <li>Python</li>
      <li>JavaScript</li>
      <li>TypeScript</li>
      <li>SQL</li>
      <li>Bash</li>
      <li>CFML</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>AI &amp; Automation</h3>
    <ul class="skill-list">
      <li>AI-Assisted Engineering Workflows</li>
      <li>RAG (Amazon Bedrock)</li>
      <li>AI Agents</li>
      <li>MCP Servers</li>
      <li>Vector Search &amp; Embeddings</li>
      <li>Prompt Engineering</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Backend &amp; APIs</h3>
    <ul class="skill-list">
      <li>Node.js</li>
      <li>REST APIs</li>
      <li>AWS Lambda</li>
      <li>API Gateway</li>
      <li>Serverless Architecture</li>
      <li>Distributed Systems</li>
      <li>Event-Driven Architecture</li>
      <li>Real-Time Streaming</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Frontend</h3>
    <ul class="skill-list">
      <li>React</li>
      <li>HTML/CSS</li>
      <li>Responsive Web Applications</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Cloud &amp; Infrastructure</h3>
    <ul class="skill-list">
      <li>EC2</li>
      <li>Elastic Beanstalk</li>
      <li>Lambda</li>
      <li>RDS</li>
      <li>Aurora</li>
      <li>S3</li>
      <li>CloudFront</li>
      <li>ECS</li>
      <li>EKS</li>
      <li>Cognito</li>
      <li>Amplify</li>
      <li>Kinesis</li>
      <li>VPC</li>
      <li>IAM</li>
      <li>CloudWatch</li>
      <li>CloudFormation</li>
      <li>AWS SAM</li>
      <li>Terraform</li>
      <li>Docker</li>
      <li>Kubernetes</li>
      <li>Helm</li>
      <li>Linux</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Databases &amp; Data</h3>
    <ul class="skill-list">
      <li>MySQL</li>
      <li>Aurora</li>
      <li>DynamoDB</li>
      <li>Redshift</li>
      <li>ElastiCache (Redis/Valkey)</li>
      <li>SQL Server</li>
      <li>AWS Glue</li>
      <li>Athena</li>
      <li>Apache Iceberg</li>
      <li>Data Modeling</li>
      <li>Data Vault</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Security &amp; Governance</h3>
    <ul class="skill-list">
      <li>AWS Organizations</li>
      <li>IAM &amp; Identity Center</li>
      <li>GuardDuty</li>
      <li>Security Hub</li>
      <li>AWS Config</li>
      <li>KMS</li>
      <li>Secrets Manager</li>
      <li>PCI Compliance</li>
      <li>Zero Trust</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Tools &amp; Testing</h3>
    <ul class="skill-list">
      <li>Git</li>
      <li>GitHub Actions</li>
      <li>CI/CD Pipelines</li>
      <li>Playwright</li>
      <li>pytest</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Leadership &amp; Operations</h3>
    <ul class="skill-list">
      <li>Hiring &amp; Onboarding</li>
      <li>Mentoring &amp; Coaching</li>
      <li>Performance Management</li>
      <li>Delivery Ownership</li>
      <li>Incident Response</li>
      <li>IT Service Management</li>
      <li>Change Management</li>
      <li>Budget Management</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="resume-section" aria-labelledby="experience-heading">
    <h2 id="experience-heading">Work Experience</h2>

    <article class="experience-item">
      <h3>Staff Engineer</h3>
      <p class="experience-meta">
        <span class="company">National Testing Network</span>
        <span class="separator" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
        <time datetime="2020">2020</time> &ndash; Present
      </p>
      <ul class="experience-details">
        <li>Led and contributed to the rewrite of a legacy candidate portal as a mobile-friendly serverless application using React, Python, AWS Lambda, API Gateway, DynamoDB, and RDS; designed a new sign-up flow that increased registrations by approximately 20%</li>
        <li>Designed, secured, and operated production AWS infrastructure spanning RDS, EC2, ECS, EKS, IAM, VPC networking, load balancers, CloudFront, and serverless workloads</li>
        <li>Architected and maintained a multi-engine AWS data platform spanning Aurora, Aurora Serverless, RDS MySQL/PostgreSQL, Redshift, DynamoDB, and ElastiCache for business-critical applications serving thousands of users</li>
        <li>Introduced Kiro and structured AI-assisted and agentic development workflows, accelerating feature delivery by approximately 60% while improving code quality and production stability</li>
        <li>Built reusable JavaScript test libraries and Markdown-based Playwright guidance for AI coding agents, improving generated end-to-end test accuracy by an estimated 70%</li>
        <li>Built an internal RAG assistant using Amazon Bedrock, enabling retrieval of current information about job postings and candidate pools; tuned parameters to improve response consistency</li>
        <li>Engineered a remote proctoring platform in three weeks using Python, TypeScript, APIs, and Amazon Kinesis Video Streams, replacing a vendor solution projected to cost $50,000 and enabling continued operations during COVID-19 disruptions</li>
        <li>Designed and implemented a video interview recording platform using LiveKit, Node.js, TypeScript, Kubernetes (EKS), and Helm, used by thousands of candidates and public safety agencies</li>
        <li>Built a middleware integration layer using Python to bridge legacy toolsets with the Amazon RDS Data API, streamlining developer tooling and database administration workflows</li>
        <li>Built a data lake and analytics platform using AWS Glue, Athena, Spark, Parquet, S3, Redshift, QuickSight, and Data Vault modeling to support operational reporting and business analysis</li>
        <li>Implemented ElastiCache for Redis and Valkey (including Serverless) to provide distributed session caching across ephemeral Elastic Beanstalk, container, and serverless instances</li>
        <li>Migrated manual RDS infrastructure to CloudFormation, designed separation-of-concerns stacks, and built a data copy service using ECS, Python, EventBridge, and RDS for PII-sanitized developer environments</li>
        <li>Tuned SQL, indexes, execution plans, and connection behavior across transactional workloads, improving database performance by approximately 40%</li>
        <li>Created separate AWS development environments and governance controls using AWS Organizations, IAM Identity Center, GuardDuty, Security Hub, and AWS Config</li>
        <li>Implemented infrastructure as code and deployment automation using CloudFormation, AWS SAM, Terraform, GitHub Actions, and Python</li>
        <li>Owned major products and features from ambiguous stakeholder requirements through implementation, production deployment, and iterative improvement</li>
        <li>Created architecture documentation, operational procedures, security policies, development standards, and technical knowledge resources</li>
        <li>Established and oversaw AI governance workgroup and advisory board, establishing AI use policies and tools</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="experience-item">
      <h3>Senior Engineer &amp; Engineering Manager</h3>
      <p class="experience-meta">
        <span class="company">National Testing Network</span>
        <span class="separator" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
        <time datetime="2015">2015</time> &ndash; <time datetime="2020">2020</time>
      </p>
      <ul class="experience-details">
        <li>Built the company's AWS platform from the ground up, migrating a fragile single-server ColdFusion/MySQL environment to Lucee, Elastic Beanstalk, and managed RDS; improved uptime by approximately 80%, performance by approximately 60%, and reduced hosting and licensing costs</li>
        <li>Built and scaled the engineering and IT teams by approximately 150%; established internal infrastructure, engineering, and reporting teams with clear ownership and accountability</li>
        <li>Hired and mentored engineering and infrastructure personnel while establishing expectations for production ownership, security, documentation, and continuous improvement</li>
        <li>Established software development, change management, IT service management, information security, PCI compliance, and production support processes as the organization grew by approximately 125%</li>
        <li>Managed production infrastructure, applications, databases, identity systems, endpoint services, vendors, and operational support while remaining a hands-on engineer delivering features across UI, backend, and database layers</li>
        <li>Owned CloudWatch monitoring, alerting, incident response, root cause analysis, capacity planning, and cost/performance optimization across application and data layers</li>
        <li>Led incident response and complex troubleshooting across AWS, Linux, databases, applications, networking, identity platforms, and third-party integrations</li>
        <li>Established database reliability standards using Multi-AZ architectures, automated snapshots, point-in-time recovery, disaster recovery runbooks, and production change controls</li>
        <li>Designed and implemented on-premises network, security (SonicWall, OSSEC), site-to-site VPNs, hybrid cloud infrastructure, and private DNS</li>
        <li>Led PCI compliance initiatives, security controls, identity management, and governance programs</li>
        <li>Implemented least-privilege IAM policies, role-based access controls, Cognito authentication, encryption, and credential management for systems processing sensitive candidate and payment information</li>
        <li>Migrated customer service team from an expensive call center service to Amazon Connect, saving $12,000 per year while enabling modern features</li>
        <li>Migrated company email from legacy POP3 to Google Workspace, enabling real-time collaboration, eliminating spam, and improving security posture</li>
        <li>Designed and implemented company-wide remote work policies, procedures, and infrastructure including remote security and automated remediation</li>
        <li>Participated in RFP responses and security audits with government agencies</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="experience-item">
      <h3>Senior Web Developer</h3>
      <p class="experience-meta">
        <span class="company">National Testing Network</span>
        <span class="separator" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
        <time datetime="2013">2013</time> &ndash; <time datetime="2015">2015</time>
      </p>
      <ul class="experience-details">
        <li>Designed, developed, and maintained multiple customer-facing and internal web applications across the UI, backend, and database layers using multiple languages and frameworks</li>
        <li>Built a custom multi-tenant licensing platform supporting registration and testing workflows for public safety agencies, licensing organizations, and candidates</li>
        <li>Standardized Git-based development practices and built internal frameworks and reusable APIs, improving development speed by approximately 25%</li>
        <li>Created an on-premises virtual environment hosting the company's first Git repositories, CI/CD pipeline, ticketing system, and internal development services</li>
        <li>Developed backend applications, APIs, payment workflows, database systems, and operational automation supporting high-volume public-facing services</li>
        <li>Created custom Linux-based secure testing kiosks distributed nationwide for secure testing by public safety candidates</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="experience-item">
      <h3>Software Developer &amp; Part-Time Database Instructor</h3>
      <p class="experience-meta">
        <span class="company">Everett Community College</span>
        <span class="separator" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
        <time datetime="2005">2005</time> &ndash; <time datetime="2013">2013</time>
      </p>
      <ul class="experience-details">
        <li>Developed and supported public-facing and internal production applications while maintaining approximately 99.9% availability</li>
        <li>Built database-driven applications using CFML, SQL Server, and JavaScript with a focus on maintainability, usability, and performance</li>
        <li>Supported Linux servers, virtualization, databases, load-balanced web platforms, authentication services, identity provisioning, and multi-site network environments</li>
        <li>Helped migrate approximately 5,000 users to Google Apps and integrated account provisioning with Novell Identity Manager</li>
        <li>Installed and maintained network equipment including Cisco switches, routers, bandwidth management, and security appliances</li>
        <li>Implemented Splunk and OSSEC for reliability, performance, and security monitoring and alerting</li>
        <li>Designed and taught database design and Microsoft SQL Server fundamentals courses as a part-time instructor</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="resume-section" aria-labelledby="education-heading">
    <h2 id="education-heading">Education</h2>
    <p><strong>B.S. Cloud and Network Engineering</strong> &mdash; Western Governors University (Expected August 2026)</p>
  </section>

  <section class="resume-section" aria-labelledby="certifications-heading">
    <h2 id="certifications-heading">Certifications</h2>
    <ul class="certification-list">
      <li><strong>AWS Certified SysOps Administrator – Associate</strong><span class="cert-date">2025</span></li>
      <li><strong>AWS Certified Developer – Associate</strong><span class="cert-date">2025</span></li>
      <li><strong>ITIL Foundation</strong><span class="cert-date">2024</span></li>
      <li><strong>CompTIA Security+</strong><span class="cert-date">2024</span></li>
      <li><strong>CompTIA Cloud+</strong><span class="cert-date">2023</span></li>
      <li><strong>AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner</strong><span class="cert-date">2023</span></li>
      <li><strong>CompTIA Project+</strong><span class="cert-date">2023</span></li>
      <li><strong>CompTIA Network+</strong><span class="cert-date">2023</span></li>
      <li><strong>Linux Essentials (LPI)</strong><span class="cert-date">2022</span></li>
      <li><strong>CompTIA A+</strong><span class="cert-date">2022</span></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .resume-section {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .resume-section h2 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .resume-section p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .resume-section p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .resume-section h3 {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .skill-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .skill-list li {
    background-color: var(--color-bg-alt);
    padding: var(--space-xs) var(--space-md);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .experience-item {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .experience-item h3 {
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .experience-meta {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .experience-meta .company {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .experience-meta .separator {
    margin-inline: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .experience-details {
    padding-left: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .experience-details li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    max-width: var(--content-max-width);
  }

  .certification-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .certification-list li {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    padding: var(--space-sm) 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .certification-list li:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .cert-date {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-left: var(--space-md);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .skill-list {
      gap: var(--space-xs);
    }
  }
</style>
